*
* Schottky diodes: lower Vf (~0.3V vs 0.6V), faster switching.
* Key differentiator: EG=0.69 (vs 1.11 Si), XTI=2 (vs 3 Si).
* Common in power supply protection and high-speed switching.
*
* Sources: MicroCode Engineering, International Rectifier datasheets

